## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                  ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                   ← builds the Koa app; separate from main.ts so tests can import it directly
├── config/env.ts            ← the only file that reads process.env
├── errors/app-error.ts      ← domain-agnostic error classes (AppError, NotFoundError, ValidationError)
├── middlewares/              ← error handling, validation glue
├── shared/                   ← database/cache clients used by more than one module
└── features/<module>/
    ├── <module>.routes.ts              ← wires everything (manual DI)
    ├── commands/                       ← write-path: Create, Update, Delete
    ├── queries/                        ← read-path: GetById, List
    ├── domain/                         ← entity, repository interface, domain events
    ├── infrastructure/                 ← bus, controller, per-ORM repositories
    └── dto/                            ← request validation, response shapes
```

## CQRS flow

```
HTTP request → Router → Controller → CommandBus/QueryBus → Handler → Repository/ORM

POST   /product  →  CreateProductController  →  CommandBus.execute(CreateProductCommand)
                                                 →  CreateProductHandler.execute(command)
                                                 →  Repository.save(entity)
                                                 →  ProductCreatedEvent

GET    /product/:id →  GetProductController  →  QueryBus.execute(GetProductQuery)
                                                 →  GetProductHandler.execute(query)
                                                 →  Repository.findById(id)
                                                 →  ProductResponseDto
```

Commands mutate state and return domain events. Queries read state and return DTOs — never the other way around.

